{
  "subtype": "faceted_decomposition",
  "concept": "incident_inefficiency_reasons",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "resolution_time_hours",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "restatement",
      "rationale": "This measures the magnitude/outcome of resolution inefficiency (how long it took), not a REASON for it. It is essentially a metric of the inefficiency itself rather than a constitutive aspect of why inefficiency occurs."
    },
    {
      "name": "issue_type",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "The category of underlying issue (printer, network, software, database, etc.) is a genuine constitutive facet of 'what recurring issues drive inefficiency' -- it decomposes the reasons by the nature/source of the problem."
    },
    {
      "name": "is_repeat_issue",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Whether an incident is a recurring/repeat issue is a legitimate aspect of the recurring-issue reason space; recurrence itself is a constitutive facet of inefficiency drivers directly tied to 'recurring issues' in the query."
    },
    {
      "name": "above_avg_resolution",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "restatement",
      "rationale": "A binary flag for above-average resolution time is a derived thresholding of resolution_time_hours -- it restates the inefficiency outcome, not a reason for it, and overlaps with resolution_time_hours."
    }
  ],
  "facet_columns": ["issue_type", "is_repeat_issue"],
  "non_facet_columns": ["resolution_time_hours", "above_avg_resolution"],
  "mutual_exclusivity": 0.4,
  "exhaustiveness": 0.3,
  "rationale": "Only two of the four added columns (issue_type, is_repeat_issue) are constitutive facets of the 'reasons' concept. resolution_time_hours and above_avg_resolution measure the inefficiency OUTCOME rather than its causes/parts, and they overlap heavily with each other (the binary flag is a derived threshold of the hours), lowering mutual exclusivity. The genuine facets also fail to cover major reason dimensions that would explain WHY resolution is inefficient -- e.g., process/handoff factors (reassignments, escalations), staffing/ownership, priority/SLA breaches, information completeness, and wait vs. work time. Coverage of the concept's constitutive reason-aspects is therefore weak."
}

